      "writtenOn": "2023-03-07T21:10:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This just feels wrong. The IpConfiguration is only null when interface state is absent. An absent interface is not tracked by EthernetTracker and therefore cannot have an IpConfiguration. Additionally, this change creates a discrepancy between the behavior of broadcastInterfaceStateChange and unicastInterfaceStateChange. Not to mention that if you want to change the behavior of the callbacks, you will have to put it behind an SDK version / extension version check to not break existing apps.",
